  {
   "id": "a1-questions",
   "title": "Asking Questions",
   "level": "A1",
   "unit": "First Steps",
   "summary": "Yes/no questions and question words: what, where, when, who, how.",
   "explanation": "Yes/no questions: with 'to be', invert: 'Is he here?'. With other verbs, use do/does: 'Do you work here?'\nQuestion words: what (thing), where (place), when (time), who (person), why (reason), how (manner), how much (price/uncountable), how many (countable), how old (age), what time.\nWord order: question word + do/does/be + subject + verb: 'Where do you live?' 'What time does the train leave?' 'How old are you?'\nFrench speakers: don't forget do/does: *Where you live? → Where do you live?",
