     "s": "Professor",
     "t": "From a purely rational perspective, the price you originally paid is irrelevant. What matters is the expected future return of each investment."
    },
    {
     "s": "Professor",
     "t": "But psychologically, selling a losing position means admitting the loss, turning a paper loss into a real one, and that is precisely what loss-averse investors try to avoid."
    },
    {
     "s": "Professor",
     "t": "I should stress that loss aversion is not irrational in every context. In environments where losses can be catastrophic, caution may well be adaptive."
    },
